    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "R4g0a",
      "x": 2000,
      "y": 170,
      "name": "E - Decisions",
      "width": 620,
      "fill": "#f4eedf",
      "cornerRadius": 12,
      "stroke": {
        "align": "inside",
        "thickness": 1,
        "fill": "#d8c9a6"
      },
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 20,
      "padding": 28,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "CaEPZ",
          "name": "dt",
          "fill": "#1a1612",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Decisions that drive the implementation",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 26,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "TFZpQ",
          "name": "ds",
          "fill": "#6f6353",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Mobile only (< md / 768px). Desktop side-by-side panels and the desktop tour are untouched.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Mscf4",
          "name": "k1",
          "fill": "#9c7a2e",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "1 · THE EXIT GETS A LABEL — SUPERSEDES #7222 DECISION 2",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 0.6
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "aF5yR",
          "name": "v1",
          "fill": "#1a1612",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "“‹ Return to file preview”, gold, min-h-44, top-left of the takeover header. #7222 shipped a bare 44×44 chevron; on a surface that covers the whole phone the only affordance out should say where it goes. aria-label matches the visible text — no more “Back to document”.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Kgios",
          "name": "k2",
          "fill": "#9c7a2e",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2 · ONE HEADER, NOT THREE",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 0.6
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VZyCh",
          "name": "v2",
          "fill": "#1a1612",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "KbChatContent's own header (filename + ✕) is suppressed inside the takeover: it repeats the filename the takeover header already shows and adds a SECOND dismiss control. It stays on desktop, where it is the only close affordance. The C4 “ask the Concierge” hint stays — it is the one line that is not a duplicate.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "igdcB",
          "name": "k3",
          "fill": "#9c7a2e",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "3 · THE CHAT COLUMN FILLS THE TAKEOVER",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 0.6
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ZoWkv",
          "name": "v3",
          "fill": "#1a1612",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "c4-workspace wraps KbChatContent in a plain h-full div, which is display:block — the child's flex-1 has no flex parent to resolve against, so the column stops at content height and leaves half a phone empty. Becomes a flex column. Same bug, same fix, on the Code tab wrapper.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "960et",
          "name": "k4",
          "fill": "#9c7a2e",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "4 · THE TRIGGER SHORTENS; THE BREADCRUMB YIELDS",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 0.6
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "0sxyB",
          "name": "v4",
          "fill": "#1a1612",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Two independent fixes, because either alone still breaks: the header's left group gets min-w-0 so KbBreadcrumb truncates instead of shoving, AND the gold pill gets shrink-0 with a short visible label (“Ask” / “Continue”) below md. Full label at md+. The accessible name never shortens.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "XFZuQ",
          "name": "k5",
          "fill": "#9c7a2e",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "5 · NO KEYBOARD CHORD IN A TOUCH PLACEHOLDER",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 0.6
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VIZAd",
          "name": "v5",
          "fill": "#1a1612",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "“Ask about this document — Ctrl+Shift+L to quote selection” wraps past the rows=1 / min-h-36 textarea and is cut mid-glyph. Below md the chord is dropped: it names a shortcut a phone cannot press.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "OmLXM",
          "name": "k6",
          "fill": "#9c7a2e",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "6 · THE TOUR SPOTLIGHT COMES BACK ON MOBILE",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 0.6
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "JSyJO",
          "name": "v6",
          "fill": "#1a1612",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "guided-tour.tsx blanket-nulls the rect below 768px, so all 19 steps are a centred card over a flat scrim. The rule predates the action:* steps — ten of them target in-page anchors that are fully on screen on a phone. It goes; measure() already rejects absent, zero-area and off-screen targets on its own, which is exactly what the seven nav-tab steps need.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "mWRg3",
          "name": "k7",
          "fill": "#9c7a2e",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "7 · NAV-TAB STEPS OPEN THE DRAWER THEY TALK ABOUT",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 0.6
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "5Rldj",
          "name": "v7",
          "fill": "#1a1612",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "“Click the Inbox tab” points into a closed drawer. Those seven steps reuse the EXISTING `reveal` event mechanism (already used by the New Issue dialog) to open the nav drawer while the step is active and close it on the way out. The layout handler ignores the open below md only — on desktop drawerOpen would make the main content inert.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "btEAb",
          "name": "k8",
          "fill": "#9c7a2e",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "8 · THE CARD GOES BELOW THE TARGET, NOT BESIDE IT",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "700",
          "letterSpacing": 0.6
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "cawBk",
          "name": "v8",
          "fill": "#1a1612",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "anchoredCardStyle only tries right-then-left. A phone target is full-bleed, so both fail and the card lands ON the thing it is pointing at. Order becomes: right, left, below, above, then clamp. Desktop keeps hitting the right branch first, so its placement does not move.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "cp5Sm",
          "name": "rj",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "fill": "#f7e6e4",
          "cornerRadius": 10,
          "stroke": {
            "align": "inside",
            "thickness": 1,
            "fill": "#d9a9a4"
          },
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 16,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "pKqtr",
              "name": "rjt",
              "fill": "#a03c36",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "REJECTED — A SECOND FLOATING “ASK” FAB",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "700",
              "letterSpacing": 0.6
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "iuEql",
              "name": "rjb",
              "fill": "#7a3b37",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Would dodge the header overflow without fixing it, and #7222 decision 3 already settled that ONE trigger drives both the markdown sidebar and the C4 Concierge. A FAB also floats over diagram content on the one screen where the canvas is the point. Rejected — the header group is fixed instead.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "tsadZ",
          "name": "ft",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "fill": "#ede4cc",
          "cornerRadius": 10,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 16,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "8D4lE",
              "name": "ftt",
              "fill": "#7a5e1f",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "FILES THIS TOUCHES",
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "700",
              "letterSpacing": 0.6
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "GJydH",
              "name": "ftb",
              "fill": "#5c5043",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "components/chat/kb-chat-fullscreen.tsx — labelled exit, compact context line\ncomponents/chat/kb-chat-content.tsx — suppress own header in the takeover; drop the chord below md\ncomponents/kb/c4-workspace.tsx — flex the tab-panel wrappers\ncomponents/kb/kb-content-header.tsx — min-w-0 on the left group, shrink-0 on the actions\ncomponents/kb/kb-chat-trigger.tsx — short visible label below md, full accessible name\ncomponents/kb/kb-breadcrumb.tsx — truncate\ncomponents/tour/guided-tour.tsx — drop the breakpoint kill; below/above card fallback\ncomponents/tour/tour-steps.ts + tour-provider.tsx — reveal the nav drawer on tab steps\napp/(dashboard)/layout.tsx — honour the drawer-reveal event below md only",
              "lineHeight": 1.7,
              "fontFamily": "Inter",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "It0tg",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 1030,
      "name": "lA",
      "fill": "#7a5e1f",
      "content": "A · BEFORE — three bars of chrome, chat does not fill",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "mwS1I",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 1030,
      "name": "lB",
      "fill": "#7a5e1f",
      "content": "B · AFTER — one header, labelled exit, chat fills",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "FuOLA",
      "x": 1040,
